"""Admit finite Candidate007 checks, preserving the proof's earlier state."""
from pathlib import Path
from datetime import datetime,timezone
from hashlib import sha256
import json
from flint import arb
now=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds')
base=Path('research/91_candidate_checkpoint_audit');root=next((base/'verification').glob('N500_*'))
x=json.loads((root/'checks.json').read_text());s=json.loads((root/'statistics_checks.json').read_text())
assert x['maximum_order']==500 and x['poisson_all_residuals_contain_zero'] and x['poisson_checked_coefficients']==1252500
assert x['canonical_zero_modes']==500 and x['exact_parameter_and_leading_profile_checks']==12
assert s['all_checks_pass'] and s['checkpoint_sha256']==x['checkpoint_sha256']
assert all(row['all_coefficients_resolved'] and row['uncertain_zero_midpoints']==0 for row in x['fields'].values())
assert sum(row['coefficient_count'] for row in x['fields'].values())==2505500
ledger=Path('VERIFY_REPORT.md');text=ledger.read_text();assert '## V551 ' in text and '## V552 ' not in text
def ref(p):return dict(path=str(p),sha256=sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest())
p=base/'PROOF.md';(root/'sources/PROOF_before_V552.md').write_bytes(p.read_bytes());proof=p.read_text()
proof=proof.replace('Status: finite input, precision and differential Poisson checks confirmed through410 (V224).','Status: finite input, precision and differential Poisson checks confirmed through 500 (V552).')
proof+=f'''\n## Finite extension through 500, admitted {now}\n\nV552 confirms the exact parameter and all ten leading coefficients, resolution of all 2,505,500 stored density and stream coefficients, every 1,252,500 differential Poisson coefficient and 500 zero stream means. The audit uses 2304-bit arithmetic on the producer's 2048-bit checkpoint. No source uncertainty is discarded. Its actual runtime was{x['actual_elapsed_s']:.6f}seconds.\n\nAt 500 the density l1 coefficient root is 3.5113304338278596773, its coefficient l2 root is 3.4990193030317579247, and the maximum-coefficient root is 3.4953383230852649907. The last maximum is at frequency 155. All reported four-decimal root values at400,450,480 and 500 agree. The independent finite least-squares fit on250..500 gives L=3.6560389182384892449 with RMS0.7169934133332399743, and the ten-step smoothed ratio is3.5188627251889768052 at 500. These are finite statistics, not an asymptotic law. The statistics check took{s['actual_elapsed_s']:.6f}seconds.\n\nThe producer's normalized-division monitor is log10 radius=-301.1999370973300884. This differs from the largest individual coefficient relative radius, approximately4.10e-300 across both fields; both are small, and they measure different quantities. The all-order convergence question at the exact stored rational parameter remains open. The independent nonlinear audit still reaches only its separately admitted selected orders, including410. The input remains in the read-only peer checkpoint and is identified by its SHA256 in the receipts; no additional1.55GB copy was made.\n''';p.write_text(proof)
snapshot=root/'sources/PROOF_at_V552.md';snapshot.write_text(proof)
admission=dict(admitted_at_utc=now,ledger='V552',verdict='CONFIRMED_FINITE_ONLY',maximum_order=500,checkpoint_sha256=x['checkpoint_sha256'],input_and_poisson=ref(root/'checks.json'),statistics=ref(root/'statistics_checks.json'),proof=ref(snapshot),scope='Finite exact-input, precision, norm, Poisson and displayed-statistic checks; no infinite convergence or full nonlinear prefix conclusion.')
(root/'admission.json').write_text(json.dumps(admission,indent=2)+'\n')
with ledger.open('a') as f:f.write(f'''\n\n## V552 | {now} | Candidate007 finite checkpoint and statistics through 500\n\n**Claim.** The final 2048-bit Candidate007 checkpoint through 500 retains the exact prescribed inputs, resolved coefficient intervals, differential Poisson consistency and the newly reported finite root and fit statistics.\n\n**Method.** Decode the dyadic intervals independently, check exact input inclusion, sum norms and differentiate the Poisson identity at2304 bits. Recompute the maximum-coefficient root, normalized-division precision monitor, ten-step ratios and the two-parameter least-squares fit without importing the producer's statistics code.\n\n**Result.** All2,505,500 coefficient precision checks,1,252,500 Poisson coefficients,500 zero stream means and12 input checks pass. At 500 the density l1, coefficient l2 and maximum-coefficient roots are3.5113304338278596773,3.4990193030317579247 and3.4953383230852649907. The fit over250..500 gives L=3.6560389182384892449 and RMS0.7169934133332399743; the smoothed ratio at 500 is3.5188627251889768052. The reported monitor -301.1999371 agrees. Actual calculation times are{x['actual_elapsed_s']:.6f} and{s['actual_elapsed_s']:.6f}seconds.\n\n**Verdict: CONFIRMED for the stated finite checks; OPEN for an infinite convergence or asymptotic growth conclusion.** This does not extend the independent nonlinear checks beyond their separately admitted orders. Evidence: research/91_candidate_checkpoint_audit/PROOF.md and verification/{root.name}/admission.json.\n''')
notes=f'''## {now} VERIFIER -> TEAM: V552 Candidate007 N500 checks pass\n\nThe final 2048-bit checkpoint hash is{x['checkpoint_sha256']}. Independent2304-bit checks pass for all 2,505,500 coefficient intervals,1,252,500 differential Poisson coefficients and the exact inputs. All printed N500 roots and the400/450/480 root values agree. The maximum-coefficient root is 3.4953383230852649907 at frequency 155; fit L=3.6560389182384892449, RMS0.7169934133332399743, smoothed ratio3.5188627251889768052. Normalized-division monitor -301.1999371 also agrees.\n\nThese are finite checks. The independent nonlinear audit still reaches410 until a separate N500 check is completed. No all-order convergence or limiting L is established. Evidence91/verification/{root.name}/admission.json; no full checkpoint copy was added.\n\n'''
p=Path('NOTES_FOR_TEAM.md');p.write_text(notes+p.read_text())
p=Path('VERIFY_SUMMARY.md');t=p.read_text();t+='\nV552 extends the Candidate007 exact-input, resolved-interval, norm and differential Poisson audits through 500. Its l1 root3.5113304338 and finite ratio-fit L3.6560389182 are confirmed as finite statistics. They do not decide convergence at its stored rational parameter.\n';p.write_text(t)
with Path('WORKLOG.md').open('a') as f:f.write(f'\n{now}: V552 admits the finite Candidate007 audit through 500, including all printed roots, normalized monitor and finite ratio fit. The main audit took{x["actual_elapsed_s"]:.6f}s and the statistics check{s["actual_elapsed_s"]:.6f}s.\n')
print(now,'V552 admitted',str(root))
